Backport: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/commit/bf599a721784849e350c18ff703c9e75de939e0d
Upstream PR #127284 (v2026.9.1): fix(agents): tolerate replaced thinking catalog owners.

Before each embedded run, the reply runner checks whether the selected model
accepts images. When the running config gives that model no `input`, the check
reads a provider-scoped read-only catalog. v2026.8.1 throws
PreparedModelCatalogConfigReplacedError there when the published model runtime
belongs to another config generation than the turn. Nothing retries or fails
over, so every later turn, /new included, fails with "prepared model catalog
owner config was replaced during the read" until the gateway restarts. Upstream
skips the stale owner and builds the scoped catalog from the turn's own config.

The upstream wizard change (setup.finalize) is omitted: LobsterAI never runs the
onboarding wizard. Retire when the pinned upstream reaches v2026.9.1.

